# Caches and scratch — never worth committing
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Output. Only the running workbook is tracked, and it has to be: on a GitHub
# runner the filesystem is thrown away after every run, so jobs.xlsx *is* the
# scraper's memory of what it has already seen. Lose it and every run
# re-discovers the same jobs.
#
# Everything else output/ produces is per-run scratch — timestamped jsonl/csv,
# the rolling backup, and jobs-pending.xlsx — so it stays out.
output/*
!output/jobs.xlsx
!output/last-run.txt

# PII — the resume, whatever it happens to be named
*.pdf
*.docx
